window.EPISODE_CONTENT = [{"number":1,"title":"Why Games and Movies Based on Novels Can Expand the Story Without Replacing the Original","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Some of the most successful games and films are adapted from novels. While guaranteeing a well-built world and complete main story, the best adaptations do much more than simply retell an existing story. The works need to introduce new characters, locations, events, visuals and gameplay for the game field while respecting the original source material. These do not replace the novel but rather enhance the universe created by the novel and encourage the viewer to experience other media related to the inspirational work. It is this capability of changing and adding to the fictional universe while keeping the initial story intact that makes adaptations extremely powerful."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-01-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Hogwarts Legacy (official cover)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.hogwartslegacy.com/media"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"A novel usually contains a limited number of characters, events and world description. Films and games, on the other hand, have the opportunity to explore side stories, depict the world using visuals and create interactions with significantly more characters and world, especially in games. This expands the existing universe without changing the core setting established by the author. Hogwarts Legacy, developed by Avalanche Software, is a strong example. Although the game is set in the Harry Potter world, a successful fictional series created by J. K. Rowling, it takes place nearly a century before the original story. The game was praised for its combat, world design, characters, variety of content, and faithfulness to the source material. Another example is The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt, holding more than 200 awards and game of the year titles. While heavily inspired by the original series The Witcher, it introduced many new areas such as Velen, White Orchard, and Skellige with much more description than the books. The story fits perfectly with the source story, despite not being included in the novels. By carefully respecting the original world build and storytelling and introducing many mechanics as well as locations, these adaptations make fictional worlds feel much more alive."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-01-02.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.thewitcher.com/mt/en/witcher3"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Frequently, adaptation works introduce new characters as protagonists or supporting roles. The additions succeed when they respect the original work’s theme and rules. These characters can be  supporters for the main character when introducing an entirely new world, help with their developments, expand the side story and sometimes let the audience experience a popular work from a fresh start with a different perspective and background. The animated series Cyberpunk: Edgerunners, while still taking place in Night City, similarly to Cyberpunk 2077- the original game developed by CD Project Red- introduces a brand new protagonist, David Martinez, and the crews. The story was written by CD Project Red themselves, with tragic events and perfect depiction of Night City. The anime was considered one of the most successful animated series in the century. In some cases, adaptations take a side character to be its main perspective. This storytelling technique while keeping all the benefits of creating new characters, also uses a familiar yet resourceful fictional person. Furthermore, this story can illustrate the relationship and how others view the protagonist. For example, Better Call Saul, a spin-off from Breaking Bad, developed complex characters who have limited screen time in the original TV series. Not only does it expand the universe while remaining consistent with the original story and timeline, Better Call Saul adds emotional depth to a character audiences already knew and loved."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-01-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Cyberpunk: Edgerunners"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.cyberpunk.net/en/edgerunners"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-01-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Better Call Saul"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt3032476/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In the gaming industry, adaptations offer something neither novels nor films can fully achieve: player interaction. Developers must maintain transforming original story and audiences’ images of the works into interesting gameplay and mechanics while respecting the source material. This is a high risk high reward job. Being too faithful to the original story makes the game’s story uninteresting to the inspiration’s fan base, and an acceptable gameplay cannot make it any more attractive. On the other hand, creating a complex main quest but lacking connection to the writer’s plot not only creates confusion in new players but also causes protest in the fan community. In addition to storytelling, developers also have to invent new mechanics and translate fictional aspects in the source into their works. Magical abilities, mythical creatures, advanced technology, or unique combat styles described in a novel must become mechanics that players can actively use and enjoy. Despite these challenges, many outstanding adaptations prove that respectful expansion of an existing fictional world can result in some of the best-selling and most beloved games in the industry. The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt is an outstanding example. While Geralt, the novels’ protagonist, is described as a monster hunter with magic signs, the game, on the other hand, lets players experience far more than books can describe. They can prepare potions, oils, investigate monster tracks, make strategies and negotiate contracts instead of merely reading about Geralt’s work."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-01-05.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Lord Of The Rings (film series)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lord_of_the_Rings_(film_series)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"For music theme books, adaptation works are essential to fully express the author’s intention. The novels can only describe the characters’ passion and reaction for music while movies allow audiences to actually hear the songs, watch performances and experience the emotions through sound and visual. That said, music theme series are challenging to make adaptations, mostly because of their own advantage: music. The songs have to fit in the theme, made by real musicians for high quality, or it can cause disappointment, the worst thing that can come to work about music. One good example is The Phantom of the Opera which was originally a novel written by Gaston Leroux. The suspenseful setting of the novel as well as the romantic storyline were heightened in their musical and film versions through the use of great songs like \"The Music of the Night\". One more example would be Daisy Jones \u0026 The Six which was an adaptation of a novel written by Taylor Jenkins Reid into a TV show with songs that made the fictional rock band come to life."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-01-06.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Daisy Jones \u0026 The Six"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt8749198/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-01-07.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Phantom of the Opera (2004 film)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Phantom_of_the_Opera_(2004_film)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Game and movie versions of novels will be most successful if they build on, but do not substitute, the original narrative. In other words, if games develop new narratives, discover new territories of the world created by the author, design new characters that fit into the world built in the book, translate literary visions into game mechanics, keep the themes of the original story and, in addition, inspire players to read the novel, such games are sure to make the world of fiction even more complete and vivid."}]},{"number":2,"title":"Asian Horror Films Inspired by Folklore and Ancient Cultural Beliefs","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Horror is arguably one of the most popular and oldest genres in film as well as in literature. However, there are notable differences between Asian and Western horror, this can be seen not just in the atmosphere or jump scare but also can be clearly distinct from the origin of fear. While many Western writers often use tangible or scary looking monsters, ghosts and murderers, most Asian books and movies are heavily inspired by traditional folklore, religion and belief as well as traditional conception. These themes, while creating an uncomfortable atmosphere and unexplainable phenomena, reflect fear, belief and experience of past Asian people."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Asian folklore has been around since the start of society. Ancient people created horror stories as a way to cope with unexplainable phenomena at that time like sickness, natural disaster, darkness, dangerous threat and to prevent children from harming themselves. For any creator,  folklore is a resourceful material with many benefits. First of all, each country has its own distinct kind of horror story, then each area has their own fear and imagination, creating an almost endless amount of pieces for writers to exploit. Secondly, most of these stories are spirituality related, a genre that is very easy to use yet effectively makes the audience unsettled. The author can briefly describe the horror aspects, causing fear of unknowing and curiosity, or they can portray the atmosphere and backstory, building up the story. Directed by Kevin Ko, Incantation illustrates the atmosphere, cult and phenomena through found footage, making it look realistic while briefly describing or cutting off the story, keeping audiences on the edge of their seats."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-02-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Incantation"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incantation_(film)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"An interesting aspect of Asian horror is that it reflects great terror people have from each period. In many ancient East Asian countries, with outdated customs, poor health care and high death rate, it is common to encounter the unjustly dead, revenge ghosts or cursed areas. This trend can be seen in many horror movies from Japan, Korea, China, Thailand and Vietnam. This is not only a fearful character but also displays the concept of justice in a time when laws and society cannot bring justice to passed people, they will come back and haunt as revenge. Most Asian countries also have a large history of war and losses, from being invaded by other countries in Southeast Asia to civil wars in Korea, Japan and China. These painful memories create folklore and narrative that feel bitter and sorry to pass people while maintaining its horror aspects. However, different from normal folklore, this type of story needs to be respected and carefully taken inspiration from as it contains war and losses that can offend many Asians."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-02-02.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Ringu (franchise)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Ring_(franchise)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Japanese horror cinema belongs to some of the most iconic examples making use of culture, folklore and traditional story. The Ring, once famous across the globe, is influenced by the onryo figure, a vengeful spirit in Japanese culture. With long hair, white clothes and appearing silently, the fear does not come from bloody scenes or scary looking characters, but rather from anxiousness and curiosity, a popular concept in Japanese horror."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-02-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Onryo (Japanese traditional belief)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Onry%C5%8D#In_mass_media"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In addition, traditional mythology and belief of Asia have also played an essential role in creating horror stories and horror movies since it gives movie makers an opportunity to include supernatural characters and legends related to specific locations and religions. Often, authors either take direct inspiration from horror stories, modify it to fit into their world setting, or they take characters from popular mythology, make it horror, making it familiar to the audience while the horror aspects make it uncomfortable and enhance the curious experience. In Korea, urban legends about spirits, sorcerers and exorcism rituals appear throughout multiple successful movies. The Wailing, for instance, combines outdated belief, Shaman religion and other religious aspects to create a mystery horror story. Meanwhile, Thai cinema often includes concepts of karma, reincarnation and spirit origin from Buddhist and local religions. Nang Nak is a 1999 Thai supernatural horror film based on the Thai legend of Mae Nak Phra Khanong, taking place in a rural village with hidden outdated customs. The film illustrates the bitter sweet and scary love story of Mak and his passed wife, Nak."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The wailing"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-02-04.png"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt5215952/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-02-05.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Nang Nak"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nang_Nak"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Regardless of inspiration, most successful films based on Asian horror folklore demonstrate those stories suitable for modern audiences, or make changes to better enhance the experience. A popular concept is to make existing horror stories fit in with modern day and daily life, putting the audience in feeling relatable with the movie\u0027s setting. Another way is to make a non-horror tale into a disgusting story. The uncomfortable feeling mixed with familiar characters make it very popular on social media. A popular example of this is Journey to the West, the most well-known novel of Asia. Many authors have changed the story to make it feel cursed and disgusting, making the characters weird and bizarre. Another example is Ringu. While in the original, the curse is transferred through a mouth to mouth story near the fireplace, the writer has made the curse spread through video tapes, a fitting way back when the movie was produced."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-02-06.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Monkey King illustrated in Journey to the West"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Journey_to_the_West"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"A striking feature of Asian horror movies is that every country has come up with a distinct form of horror movie according to its culture and belief system. Japanese horror films are famous for their themes of revengeful souls and curses. These movies do not use much violence; rather, fear is generated in the mind through the idea that revenge can be carried out even after death. Korean horror movies generally have supernatural as well as family tragedies. Korean horror movies, unlike other horror movies, deal more with issues of grief and guilt and different belief systems.Buddhist ideas of karma and folklore play a big part in Thai horror. Some of these stories state that the supernatural occurrences can be attributed to wrongdoings, thereby emphasizing the fact that the consequences of any past deeds can never be escaped. However, on the flip side, Asian horror takes inspiration from the philosophies of Taoism and Buddhism, along with traditional folklore. Wandering souls, ancestor worship, and exorcisms are portrayed in horror movies. These multiple cultural elements are some of the numerous factors that make it difficult for Asian horror to become repetitive despite using similar supernatural elements."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-02-07.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Traditional Japanese yokai (Rokurokubi and Ubume)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.loc.gov/exhibits/ukiyo-e/image.html"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"It is not the case that most of the horror films that are considered the most famous in Asia come straight from the minds of the screen writers; on the contrary, they tend to be based on legends that existed long before filmmaking became an industry. The stories of the revengeful spirits, curses, ghosts and other supernatural creatures are the expressions of fear and beliefs of ancient communities that tried to find answers about the nature of things that were mysterious to them prior to the development of modern science. Through the years, such legends were translated to the language of modern cinema, thus turning centuries-old tales into the modern stories that not only preserve the cultural heritage but are also understandable to the local and international audience. Thus, it might be suggested that folklore is not just an instrument of inspiration for Asian horror movies; it is the source of the genre\u0027s unique identity. In that way, films based on legends of the past combine entertainment and preservation of cultural values."}]},{"number":3,"title":"Is fantasy becoming oversaturated?","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"For decades, fantasy has been one of the most beloved literature genres. From classical fantasy with different races and geographies to cyberpunk with high technology and night city, fiction has experienced through different eras and evolved since the start of literature. The Lord of the Rings, Harry Potter and A song of Ice and Fire, fantasy has captured many audiences’ love with worlds filled with magic and mythical creatures. Today, on the other hand, the genre faces multiple challenges. Thanks to online social media, which makes it easier to approach fictional resources and share stories, almost anyone can write and publish their own fantasy story. While this has created undeniable opportunities for many authors, it also led to a significant increase in the number of fantasy stories. A lot of these works, while they can differ in storytelling or insignificant aspects, tend to have a similar theme and stories. Of course, fantasy is not dying, some even argue this genre is growing, but it is becoming increasingly repetitive, making original ideas much harder to find."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-03-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Lord of the Rings (film series)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0120737/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The biggest reason for this problem perhaps is that fantasy has become overcrowded since it requires simple understanding to begin writing. Unlike historical themes where the authors have to research for their own world building or make complex plots for detective stories such as Sherlock Holmes, fiction allows writers to be completely free with their story. They are not restricted by rules, history facts or scientific accuracy. Writers can create kingdoms, magic systems, mythic creatures and entire civilizations purely from their imagination. Consequently, even with this freedom, many new authors lack the experience and imagination to actually create an original universe. There are hundreds of stories with the hero as protagonist, traveling across regions to make allies and defeat the great threat to humanity. At first, many series feel distinct as they have uncommon aspects, for example, main characters have deep story, powerful magic, blessing or support fictional creature, but as the story goes on, unless one has many ideas and interesting storytelling, most of them fall in the same path or start to make up confused plot and event. Classic fantasy setting is not bad at all, in fact, a well-built world can help authors to focus on story and character development, but it takes many attempts and failures to make the continuing story feel interesting. In Japan fantasy novel publishing, most of the works got shut down after some first books due to lack of sales. Audiences get hooked with first impressions of distinct aspects, but then they gradually get bored as the series continues; the characteristics that readers love become the side elements, mainly because it is hard to build a world and story around just some main points."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-03-02.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Sherlock Holmes (2009 film)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sherlock_Holmes_(2009_film)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Over the last decade, social media and technology have pushed this trend dramatically. Platforms such as Wattpad, Facebook, Webnovel and Archive of Our Own allow new writers to publish their works without going through traditional publish methods, which is very competitive for beginner authors. Other platforms such as TikTok, Reddit, Discord and Youtube help writers promote their work to much more readers, especially young people, than with only posters and old commercials. A fictional novel no longer requires approval of editors and publishing companies before finding its readers and gaining popularity. Many series are translated from web novels and short stories. The Beginning After the End, written by TurtleMe and illustrated by Fuyuki23, originated as a web novel before serialization in webcomic and recently as anime adaptation. The story received love from many fans online when it was still a web novel, its popularity soon attracted Tapas -a South Korean publishing house- editor. With all this help, the number of writers exploded, with thousands of new fantasy stories created every week. As a result, with no quality filter, the market is flooded by similar content."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-03-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Beginning After the End"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.crunchyroll.com/series/G24H1NWKE/the-beginning-after-the-end"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-03-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Archive of Our Own"},{"type":"source","text":"https://archiveofourown.org/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Unfortunately, quantity does not always produce quality. A lot of fantasy stories today are based on formulae that have been working well in the past. One often comes across characters with godly strength, storylines centered around chosen ones, magical academies, king demons, reincarnations, character-leveling similar to video games, dragons, and kingdoms resembling medieval Europe. None of these themes are necessarily negative as there are classics such as Harry Potter that helped establish the idea of magical schools and The Lord of the Rings that set conventions for modern fantasy. However, one needs to make changes, expand and combine these genres to create an original story with distinct elements, one that readers actually would stick to in the long run."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-03-05.png"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-03-06.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Harry Potter poster"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.warnerbros.com/movies/harry-potter-complete-8-film-collection"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Potter_(film_series)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The rise of artificial intelligence further deepens the problem. Artificial intelligence can generate ideas, worlds,  names, character and plot outline within minutes, all can be used as fantasy can contain any idea. However, its quality varies, its creativity is even worse. AI can only imitate and trace existing ideas but never create original pieces as it lacks experience, emotion and personal perspective. Furthermore, AI generated works can cause disappointment for many readers, they expect a new experience into other’s imagined worlds but instead receive a repetitive story from a machine. As AI-generated content becomes more common, readers may be exposed to an even larger number of generic fantasy stories. It is really frustrating to think that fantasy, a genre famous for its flexibility in world and story, is being used to make thousands of similar stories."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-03-07.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Sudowrite"},{"type":"source","text":"https://sudowrite.com/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"That said, fantasy itself does not stop expanding. A crowded market also reflects that this theme remains one of if not the world’s most beloved genre. With many stories produced day and night, readers not only keep their interest in magical worlds but also become more selective. High competition raises the standard rather than eliminating opportunities."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-03-08.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Impossible Creatures - Katherine Rundell"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/series/F6N/impossible-creatures/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-03-09.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Hierarchy - James Islington"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Will_of_the_Many"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"To conclude, fantasy is definitely being overdone since with the help of technology anyone can now write and publish imaginary worlds. Although this has been good for imagination, this has resulted in a great number of repetitive stories. This is why only a small number of stories have been able to distinguish themselves. The success of fantasy writing in today’s world does not lie in the invention of yet another imaginary kingdom; the success of fantasy lies in unforgettable characters, important messages, and an unforgettable narrative voice."}]},{"number":4,"title":"Why everyone should read classic fantasy","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"In today\u0027s literature, the fantasy genre has become one of the most recognized genres with several works like Harry Potter, The Lord of the Rings, and House of the Dragon being classic fantasies which have attracted many readers from across the world. Classic fantasy is not limited to magical animals, massive wars, and magic. It explains how stories are built, illustrates the characters\u0027 developments, and how complex cities, races and conflicts can be created from imagination. Classic fantasy is valuable not only for entertainment purposes but also for understanding some of the first storytelling and worldbuilding from imagination."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-04-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"House of the Dragon"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt11198330/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"It is undeniable that the greatest strength of classic fantasy is its unlimited potential of world building. While many other genres take place in real world locations, classic fantasy authors must create new universes from scratch without any role model to base them on. All successful books are packed with well written geography, history, languages, cultures and religions that describe the regions with different people and lifestyles. The Lord of the Rings by J.R.R. Tolkien is considered to be the best literary example of classical world building. Tolkien spent many years on the creation of his fantasy world Middle-earth before he started to write his books. He developed whole languages Quenya and Sindarin, a history of thousands of years of fiction, and even maps, genealogical tables, and myths, all combined to create a Middle-earth with magics and fictional creatures yet feel so complex and reasonable."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-04-02.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Lord of the Rings (film series)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0120737/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Similarly, J.K.Rowling’s Harry Potter illustrates a modern Britain with magical society hidden. The wizard world has its own towns, magical government, the Ministry of Magic, banking system as described in Gringotts, distinct sports that can only be played by wizards -Quidditch- education systems as in Hogwarts, laws to restrain exploiting magic power and much more. These works show that world building means much more than just simply inventing magic creatures and mindless combats. It is about creating a world whose fictional aspects naturally fit in with the story and characters."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-04-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Harry Potter(film series)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Potter_(film_series)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Classic fantasy is also famous for its journey undertaken by a group of characters rather than a single protagonist. This storytelling pattern allows writers to explore multiple perspectives, backgrounds and create interactions between characters while maintaining the themes of friendship, sacrifice, loyalty and cooperation. Besides, when the story only focuses on one character, it is harder to control the powerscale of the protagonist as the main character has to do everything alone and has too much strength, which can bore the audience and create a lonely feeling. The most convincing example can be found in The Lord of the Rings. Here Frodo, the main character, who is the only person capable of carrying the ring but not capable of traveling around Middle Earth to destroy it, requires help from other characters of the Fellowship belonging to different races – humans, elves, dwarves, hobbits, and a wizard with their particular abilities. At some point during the trip, the group was split up, thus forming separate opinions of each member and creating the uniqueness of the story. In a similar manner, Harry Potter is the main character, possessing hints of the fact that he is capable of defeating Voldemort using his magical powers but requires help of his friends and tutors at all times."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-04-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Harry Potter and Voldemort in the last fight - Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows - part 2"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Potter_and_the_Deathly_Hallows_%E2%80%93_Part_2"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Being some of the first written in its genre, classic fantasy appeals to audiences of all ages because of its balance between complexity and accessibility. While the main story often illustrates straightforward ideas of good versus evil, dangerous quests and travelling through the world to defeat the greatest demon, the world itself often gets described thoroughly, from the cities with different races, rules, politics and crowded markets, which commonly are the most detailed places, to forests filled with fantasy creatures, unexpected dangers and magical powers flowing. This way, readers will not lose track of the main goal because of all the detail and complex world building. In House of the Dragon, Martin deals with issues such as succession problems, civil wars, gender roles, and legitimacy in politics. Contrary to conventional fantasy where there is a clear distinction between good and bad characters, Martin\u0027s world promotes the idea of comprehending the various motives. Most of the characters believe that their actions are justified.In the same way, while The Lord of the Rings can certainly be interpreted as an adventure story, there are other deeper issues in the story that have something to do with industrialization, destruction of the environment, bravery, and power corrupting men. The One Ring serves as an embodiment of how having total power will eventually corrupt even the best of us."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-04-05.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Frodo Baggins and the One Ring - The Lord of the Rings: The Return of the King"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lord_of_the_Rings:_The_Return_of_the_King"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The influence of classic fantasy impacts far beyond just reading books. Many films, video games, tabletop games and communicating lectures take heavy techniques developed by classic fantasy writers. The way of storytelling in classic fantasy is considered one of the most important achievements in literature. The adaptation of The Lord of the Rings demonstrated that by following the method of focus on the main objective while describing the world as the group progresses completely hooked the audiences, winning 17 Academy Awards across the trilogy, including Best Picture, becoming the most well-known fantasy series of all time. Regarding the game field, franchises such as The Elder Scroll, Dragon Age and World of Warcraft all feature well developed world building, diverse races and support from other non playable characters inspired by classic fantasy works."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-04-06.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Elder Scrolls"},{"type":"source","text":"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Elder_Scrolls"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-04-07.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"World of Warcraft"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_of_Warcraft"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Reading classic fantasy is not only an experience of escape from reality. It is a chance to see how to create an interesting world, how fantasy storytelling can be so addictive, and how deep issues can be discussed in imaginary places which are still easy to understand. For those who aim to become writers, designers, critics, or just curious about a work’s movies or games, classic fantasy is a must-read genre. In all those dragons, wizards, and magical kingdoms, there lies an interesting examination of history, society, friendship, leadership, and human nature itself. This is the reason why these books are classics, and should be read by everyone."}]},{"number":5,"title":"World building inspired by culture around the world","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"One of many important aspects shaping the attractiveness in fantasy work, including literature, movies and games, is the world building of the work. This is the process of creating a fantasy world or universe that has its unique history, geography, races and sometimes politics. Therefore, creating a fantasy world from nothing is an overwork for any author. Because of that, real life culture acts as an important inspiration for any work."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In world building, culture is considered one of if not the most important aspect. It can be an ideal for language and customs, both of which can help one make detailed descriptions of different parts of their world, this creates a feeling of familiar but different, the audience can notice familiar aspects while exploring new elements. This not only makes the works feel more logical, events occur from reasonable causes, adding a complexity to the creation, but also creates a wide diversity in one’s product. An undeniable example of this is Avatar: the Last Airbender, a successful animated series. In this work, there are four main countries, each resembling a distinctive culture, the air nomads are based on Tibetan Buddhist and Shaolin monks, water tribe are inspired by Inuit and Yupik culture, earth kingdom, on the other hand, is heavily influenced by Chinese culture while fire nation are based on Japanese architecture."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-05-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Roku Temple - Avatar: The Last Airbender"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avatar:_The_Last_Airbender"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-05-02.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Kinkaku-ji, Kyoto"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_architecture"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Natural environment characteristics can act as a great base for world building. Mountains, deserts, forests, islands and rivers determine where people settle, how they obtain food, what materials they use for construction and even how they wage war. As a result, different environments naturally give rise to different cultures, traditions and lifestyles. This relationship makes a fictional world feel more believable because it reflects the way civilizations evolved throughout human history. A lot of works take inspiration from real life environment aspect to build its world: in Dune, Arrakis desert makes water the most valuable resource, forcing the people there to become warriors to bring back resources; in Game of Thrones, the northern freezing climate creates tough warriors, making the people there live a miserable life."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-05-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Arrakis desert - Dune: Part Two"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune:_Part_Two"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Architecture can be a powerful tool for any author. A construct can tell more than direct explanations, it can represent the time, geography, and lifestyle. Multi-layered curved roofs recall Asian tradition, gigantic stone castles reflect European feudalism, dirt houses show a dry environment, wood constructs can be seen near forests. Selective selection of architecture not only aesthetic but also reflects natural conditions, the technical and cultural level of the residents. This can be seen in Avatar by James Cameron, while the first movie takes place in a forest with constructions fit with terrain vegetation, tree houses and campfire in the cave, the second film revolves around coastal area, with houses and tents built near beach with palm tree and leave, with many harbors connected directly to residential."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-05-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Orava Castle in Slovakia"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feudalism"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-05-05.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Avatar: The Way of Water - promotion artwork"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avatar:_The_Way_of_Water"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"A popular principle in world building is that the military never exists independently. It\u0027s influenced by different aspects, natural geography, resources, history, races, some even more detailed because of magic or advanced technology. Although set in a fantasy world, a well built one always bases their military power and tactics on culture, a poor in resources area but having thousands of machines is unconvincing. A lot of fantasy work succeeds by carefully building its war history and relationship between races or countries, which both keep the audience interested and help build up for conflicts or describe battles. One of the most famous resembles The Lord of the Rings series, while having a rather traditional setting with races like human, elf, half-ling and dwarf, the author J. R. R Tolkien creates advantages and drawbacks to each race, humans have advanced technology and large quantities, elves are quality rangers and can use powerful magic, dwarfs are resourceful and wield great strength while halflings are fast and friendly."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-05-06.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Lord of the Rings (film series) - Main characters"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0120737/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Mythology and folklore can be a work’s inspiration, or in some cases, the story\u0027s main topic. These cultural stories can be a reliable resource for any creator regardless of their experience. Mythology and folklore are familiar and recognisable, which help both author and audience understand the story’s core, while still able to make changes and add new aspects. Additionally, these stories can be modified to fit with a wide variety of genres from heavy ones like horror or psychology to more popular ones like adventure and action. Directed by Hayao Miyazaki, Spirited Away, heavily influenced by Japanese folklore, follows the protagonist Chihiro on her journey throughout the spirit realm where folklore creatures and Studio Ghibli’s own creation take place, maintaining a familiar yet original story. A more direct influence can be seen in Ringu, a traditional horror story of Japan about onryo or revenge ghosts."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-05-07.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Spirited Away"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0245429"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-05-08.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Ringu"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ring_(film)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Religion and belief systems are one of the most influential materials in world building. Throughout history, religions have shaped the values, traditions and behaviors of many societies, with some still remaining in today\u0027s world. As a result, many fantasy creators take huge inspiration from real life beliefs to make their fictional worlds more authentic and consistent, sometimes the story revolves around religion. Rather than inventing entirely new religious systems, authors often take existing beliefs while adding original ideas. For instance, Dune incorporates ideas heavily inspired by Islam and Buddhism, creating a society where religion intertwined with politics. Similarly, The Elder Scrolls series features multiple religions and gods from Norse mythology and Greek mythology, leading to cultural diversity and political conflict between races."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-05-09.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Elder Scrolls"},{"type":"source","text":"https://elderscrolls.bethesda.net/en-US"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In conclusion, real-life cultures are super important for building a fictional world. Instead of making everything from scratch, writers often look at real cultures, environments, buildings, military traditions, myths and religions to create worlds that are both cool and believable. These real-world influences help fictional societies make sense, be diverse and feel consistent so readers can connect with the story. At the time creators can take different cultural elements and mix them in new ways making unique worlds instead of just copying real life. Many great books, movies and games show that good world building is about taking cultural foundations and turning them into new and exciting fictional worlds. This balance between reality and creativity is a reason why fantasy worlds stay in our minds for a long time. Real-life cultures help create timeless worlds."}]},{"number":6,"title":"The balance between realism and fantasy in fiction","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Sometimes, fantasy and realism are viewed as totally different techniques of storytelling. Indeed, fiction stories are known for their magical creatures, magic powers and fantasy races that cannot really occur in reality. At the same time, people seek realism in order to show the world as it is, based on laws of nature, society and human psyche. Nevertheless, many great examples of fantasy literature involve both fiction and realism. The writers make their books successful due to the skillful mixture of two types of storytelling in which readers can dive into the world of fiction and feel its emotions simultaneously. For example, the books from the Dune series and Harry Potter series are perfect examples of these opposite sides."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-06-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Dune: Part 1"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune_(2021_film)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"One of the greatest strengths of this combination is that realism offers a stable foundation for both audiences and writers. Firstly, when entering an unfamiliar fictional world, many readers often get overwhelmed and confused by new terms, cultures, races and magic systems. If every aspect of the works is completely unknown for audiences, it would be a large obstacle for them to understand or emotionally invest in the stories. Realistic elements now serve as a base understanding for readers. By turning corporate real life into a fantasy world it reduces the unfamiliar aspects of the works. Additionally, this story telling method also benefits the writer. For many, creating an original universe without guidance is near impossible. With realistic elements, however, they can lean on existing aspects to build their fictional world."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Platform 9 ¾ - Harry Potter and the Philosopher’s Stone (film)"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-06-02.png"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Potter_and_the_Philosopher\u0027s_Stone_(film)"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Dune by Frank Herbert is an exemplary story that demonstrates a perfect balance of reality and science fiction. On the surface, one would think that this story is entirely science fiction because it involves space travel, giant worms, futuristic ships, genetic engineering, and some mysterious forces that are created by the Bene Gesserit. However, there is an underlying theme of the civilization described in this book that strongly resembles various civilizations that existed at different periods in human history. Arrakis has the Fremen who resemble nomadic peoples of the desert from the Middle East and North Africa regions."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-06-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The fremen - Dune: Part 2"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fremen"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The realistic culture helps make the futuristic setting believable. While readers will come across spaceships which can travel between galaxies, they also understand the real human problems such as competition for scarce resources, political alliances, religion, loyalty to family and thirst for freedom. In many aspects, the Dune looks like an empire from history that was placed in the far future, not the completely foreign civilization. The combination of advanced technology and primitive tribes may look contradictory, however, this is the reflection of reality. Today, there are already high-tech cities together with remote tribes that keep their old customs. Herbert only amplifies the difference on the scale of the galaxy."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-06-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Peru ancient architecture"},{"type":"source","text":"https://unearththevoyage.com/15-countries-that-still-protect-ancient-ways-of-life/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The similar effect is observed in J. K. Rowling\u0027s Harry Potter where the fantasy looks even more believable because of the realistic background. There are fantastic creatures, enchanted objects, moving stairs, flying broomsticks and powerful spells in the wizarding world. However, this magical community coexists with the usual non-magic world. Harry comes from the ordinary suburban area with the Dursleys and discovers Hogwarts. Readers get the information from the point of view of Harry who learns about magic step by step."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"It is a highly effective way of telling a story since the introduction of the fantastic element happens step-by-step rather than in one go, thus, it does not shock the audience. The existence of common things like schools, families, trains, newspapers, sports games, friendship and teen problems forms the basis of the story. Even though students at Hogwarts use magic spells instead of doing their homework and studying algebra, they have to take exams, get bullied, fall in love for the first time in their lives, feel jealous, and deal with academic pressure and growing up. Such universal feelings give emotional truth to the fantastical world."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"But the realness of the fantastical universe is not limited only to physical objects and daily life. It can be seen even in the psychology of characters. No matter how strange the fictional world becomes, audiences expect the characters to react to certain situations in a human-like way. For example, heroes may have doubts, villains may have understandable motivation for their actions, while ordinary people have realistic reactions to danger and losses."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Such a rule is evident in a variety of well-written fantasy narratives. The example is given by The Lord of the Rings, where Frodo has difficulties in dealing with his responsibilities of bearing the One Ring, and eventually gets corrupted by it, portraying the psychological stresses of an average person under immense pressure. Another similar example is Eren Yeager from the manga Attack on Titan, who changes from an innocent boy longing for freedom into a morally conflicted character, whose decisions will have terrible effects. Even though their worlds include a lot of impossibilities, the process of evolution of those characters remains extremely human."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Another significant function of realism is consistency of the story. The universe created by the author does not have to comply with the laws of the reality we live in, but it must be consistent according to its rules. Once the reader understands how the magic works and how the technology of the future works, the rules must not change during the story. Consistency provides the credibility of the story. An illustration of internal consistency can be seen in the show Avatar: The Last Airbender. Though bending of the four elements may not be possible in real life, each form of bending adheres to certain rules and restrictions. It is impossible for the characters to acquire new powers without undergoing training. In time, the viewer is able to understand how the process works."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Additionally, the mixture of realism and fantasy makes thematic considerations  profound. Fantasy is not used as an escape from reality but becomes a metaphor for the problems of real life. The fight for the control over Arrakis is related to historical conflicts for oil and other natural resources, and colonialism, environmental sustainability, extremism of religion, and political manipulation are considered from the future point of view. In this manner, the novel The Hunger Games employs the concept of dystopia to shed light on such social issues as class difference, political oppression, manipulation through media, and the exploitation of entertainment. While Panem is a fictional society, the issues that it addresses bear many similarities to those present in many real societies around the world."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"This theory is also responsible for the popularity of movies such as \"Spirited Away\" and \"Princess Mononoke\" among viewers of all generations. These movies contain spirits, magic creatures, and supernatural lands, but the themes discussed in these movies are common human issues such as family, environmentalism, identity, and self-development. Although one may never encounter spirits in his/her life, he/she can definitely feel the emotions of the main characters."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In essence, there is no competition between realism and fantasy. It is the complementarity of the two genres that creates a fantastic yet plausible world of fiction. It can be Dune\u0027s historical background, the secret world of magic in Harry Potter, the complicated politics of A Song of Ice and Fire, or The Lord of the Rings\u0027 realism – the most unforgettable examples of fantasy worlds all have one thing in common. Fantasy stretches the boundaries of our imagination, but realism gives the emotional context which helps us to accept these unreal worlds as reality."}]},{"number":7,"title":"Copyright Law and the Creative Ecosystem: Protecting Authors by Protecting the Entire Industry","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Copyright law is commonly defined as the body of laws that safeguard authors from unauthorized copying and distribution of their creative work. This is indeed true; however, copyright law serves a much larger objective. Copyright law serves not just the author but the whole creative process that goes into creating the author\u0027s work. The success of each novel, movie, video game, or song is made possible by a collaborative effort between the author, editor, publisher, production studio, marketing team, lawyers, distributors, and investors. The protection of intellectual property through copyright law makes it possible for all these players to capitalize on the creative output, protect the brand, and earn money in the process."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"One of the myths is that successful creative works are created only through talented people. However, the modern world of creative industries has become quite collaborative. While a best-selling book can be written by a single author, it would take many more people to turn it into a global success: editors, literary agents, publishing houses, translators, artists, marketers, lawyers, and license negotiators among others. The same applies to blockbuster movies, which are made by thousands of people who work in various fields, from special effects to advertising."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Greatest Showman(2017)-an example of blockbuster movies"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt1485796/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Harry Potter phenomenon is a great example of this ecosystem. The books were originally written by J. K. Rowling, but the success of this series throughout the world could only be achieved because of the joint efforts of Bloomsbury Publishing, Scholastic, Warner Bros., graphic designers, translators, movie directors, video game makers, manufacturers of merchandise, and marketers. Copyright protection enabled these companies to spend billions of dollars on production of books, movies, games, theme parks, and other goods, as there was no risk that piracy could harm their business at once. Meanwhile, Rowling could focus on writing, rather than solving all commercial and legal problems connected with it herself."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-02.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The main characters trio in Harry Potterhttps://www.harrypotter.com/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"An illustration of this can be provided by The Lord of the Rings. Though the books were written by J. R. R. Tolkien, copyright protection has helped the Tolkien Estate, the publishers, New Line Cinema, Amazon MGM Studios, gaming companies, and other licensees to develop films, illustrations, video games, and merchandise based on the works in question without compromising the quality of Tolkien’s literary heritage. If there was no copyright, people could develop any unofficial versions of Tolkien’s works, which could have seriously compromised the integrity of Tolkien’s work."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-03.png"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"the Tolkien Estate trademarkNew Line Cinema logo used since"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.tolkienestate.com/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Line_Cinema"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-05.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The main cast in Fellowship Of The Ring-The Lord of the Ring movie"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0120737/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"It becomes even more apparent why copyright is so important when we take a look at the entertainment industry. The Marvel Cinematic Universe features popular superheroes like Iron Man, Captain America, and Spider-Man. But for each successful Marvel movie, there are hundreds of writers, artists, actors, engineers, special effects artists, lawyers, and businessmen who work behind the scenes. The profitability of the company does not depend only on its imagination but also on Disney\u0027s capacity to preserve their intellectual property by using copyright and trademark laws. By using licensing agreements, Marvel superheroes can be used in toys, clothes, theme parks, video games, and streaming platforms without any risk of losing control over them."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-06.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Captain America: Civil War(2016)"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt3498820/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-07.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Marvel Cinematic Universe official logo as of 2019"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.marvel.com/movies"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"One such example would be video game manufacturers. Nintendo is famous for having created many franchises throughout the world such as Super Mario, The Legend of Zelda, and Pokémon. All these games are a result of years of work by programmers, artists, writers, composers, and game designers."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-08.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Super Mario Bros."},{"type":"source","text":"https://mario.nintendo.com/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The copyright laws will help Nintendo to stop people from making and selling fake copies of their characters and game properties. Even though there are some who say that Nintendo goes too far in protecting its intellectual property, doing so helps the company to maintain its reputation and also ensure that the consumer gets the real product."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-09.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Nintendo Co., Ltd logo used since May 2016."},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.nintendo.com/us/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Copyright ensures that businesses are encouraged to make long-term investments in creative works as well. The production of a movie or AAA game may take tens of millions of dollars to develop before any money starts coming in. If investors do not see any return on their investment due to others being able to copy and sell the exact same product as soon as it is released, they are not going to invest in those projects at all. This means that copyright eliminates the risk and encourages publishers and studios to develop creative works."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Apart from providing financial security, copyright is another way of ensuring that the integrity of the creative work does not suffer at the hands of those who use it without permission. The unauthorized production or reproduction of a creative work can adversely affect the image of a franchise even though the creator himself or herself was not involved. Copyright holders can ensure the maintenance of artistic quality in authorized reproductions and derivative works. For example, Studio Ghibli is known worldwide for not only the creativity of Hayao Miyazaki but also for the way in which the studio distributes their films."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-10.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Studio Ghibli logo"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Studio_Ghibli"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Another equally valuable but less discussed benefit of copyright is that it makes it possible to delegate the responsibility to professional institutions. Once the rights to the intellectual property are legalized, publishers, production studios, licensing units, and legal departments will be responsible for numerous economic and legal processes. They will take care of contract negotiations, control the violation of copyrights, protect legal rights, license products, distribute around the world, and deal with PR issues. As a result, writers and artists will have more time for research, writing, designing, or composing than for dealing with various economic and legal aspects by themselves. While copyright will not protect anyone from the influence of public opinion and commercial success, it makes the necessary legal framework for professional institutions to do it."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-11.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild"},{"type":"source","text":"https://zelda.nintendo.com/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"With the rise of the digital economy, copyright has become even more important than before. Publishing on the Internet, streaming services, social networks, and generative artificial intelligence technologies have radically changed the range of possibilities and threats for the copyright owner. It is possible to duplicate a book, movie, song, or digital artwork and distribute it across the world in just several minutes. Without sufficient copyright protection, a creator or an investor would lose money, which would decrease their incentive to create something new. At the same time, the copyright system still develops, seeking to reconcile the interests of the copyright owner and the public."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-07-12.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Pokémon international franchise logo"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.pokemon.com/us"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"However, copyright must not be seen as an instrument that gives creators unlimited powers. All legal systems have a number of important exceptions or limitations, such as fair use/fair dealing, educational use, criticism, parody, news reporting, library archiving, etc. Such exceptions make sure that copyright benefits not only individual creators, but also serves the interests of the general public. Copyright is thus meant not to suppress creativity but to stimulate it through rewarding creators for their creativity, but at the same time letting society develop on its basis."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Ultimately, copyright law is concerned with the protection of not only the author, but the whole system of publishers, studios, investors, artists, marketers, lawyers, distributors, and technology companies that turn ideas into cultural productions on a global scale. This is proven by the examples of franchises such as Harry Potter, The Lord of the Rings, Marvel, Nintendo, and Studio Ghibli, which prove that creativity thrives when the legal and business structures are strong. Copyright law does not prevent the author from any difficulty, it rather sets the legal basis for the creative industry to operate with confidence, protect its reputation, and share tasks among specialists. Thus, it makes it possible for the author to concentrate on the things he is most skilled at: the production of new works."}]},{"number":8,"title":"Copyright Law as a Foundation for a Healthier Creative Market","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Not only is the need for talent and innovation essential to creating a flourishing market for creativity, but the need for laws that protect intellectual property is vital as well. This is accomplished through the use of copyright laws that ensure artists and publishers receive due compensation from their creations. Without this kind of copyright protection, piracy hinders investments and lowers earnings for creators while creating an uneven playing field for honest businesses versus pirates. The story of Vietnam shows how improved copyright protection has led to a different image of the market previously known for piracy."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"For many years, copyright violation was an issue which faced Vietnam. Books, translations, illegal movie streaming websites, cracked software, and copies of games could be found there. People used copyrighted material for free due to the fact that pirate versions of the material were cheaper, more convenient or just more popular than legal ones. Legal publishers had difficulties competing with those who did not incur the cost of production, licensing and marketing because it did not need any efforts."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Harry Potter books series."},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.harrypotter.com/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The problem not only influenced Vietnamese producers but also international publishers as well. In case of copyright violation, foreign companies lose incentives to localize their products, translate them into different languages and distribute them in a certain country. In that case, it was possible to see that foreign companies started to release their product with some delays or just to invest less resources in countries with a poor copyright policy. Thus, although Vietnam received foreign content, its image as the country with a high level of piracy influenced rights owners negatively."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Lord of the Rings books series."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-02.png"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lord_of_the_Rings"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The publishing industry is an excellent example of that. International books that have been a hit among their fans, including \"Harry Potter,\" \"The Lord of the Rings,\" and \"A Song of Ice and Fire,\" have taken years of effort and significant investments on the part of the authors, publishers, editors, translators, illustrators, and marketing specialists. Piracy leads to financial losses for those who produce original works, while consumers get poor-quality books that may contain mistakes during translation, poor print quality, or missing parts of the story."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"A Song of Ice and Fire-novels series"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Song_of_Ice_and_Fire"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The movie industry experiences similar problems. Movie projects, which are international in nature and are known all around the world, such as Marvel Cinematic Universe, \"Avatar,\" \"Dune,\" and Spider-Man, require investments of several hundreds of million dollars. Before copyright laws became more widespread and effective, movies were illegally copied and uploaded to the Internet immediately after their premiere in the theaters. Piracy negatively affected the box office income and did not provide strong motivation for distributors to invest in marketing and distribution in their country."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Spider-Man: Brand New Day-the Hand fight scene"},{"type":"source","text":"https://marvelanimated.fandom.com/wiki/Man-Spider"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Dune part 2-last fight scene"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-05.png"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune:_Part_Two"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Another perfect case is related to the video gaming industry. Companies like Nintendo, Sony, Microsoft, Capcom, and CD Projekt allocate huge amounts of money on the creation of unique games. Products like The Legend of Zelda, Elden Ring, Cyberpunk 2077, and Resident Evil are created in a period of years by programmers, artists, writers, musicians, and designers. The availability of cracked versions in the market just after their release leads to fewer sales. Therefore, strict copyright protection will make sure that companies recover the investments made and create more games."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-06.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Legend of Zelda: Tears Of The Kingdom"},{"type":"source","text":"https://zelda.nintendo.com/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-07.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Elden Ring DLC Shadow Of The Erdtree-official poster"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elden_Ring\\"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"It is obvious that Vietnam understands the importance of copyright and tries to establish the proper legal regime to protect copyrights. Vietnam became a participant in the most important international agreements related to copyright like the Berne Convention and the Agreement on Trade-Related Aspects of Intellectual Property Rights (TRIPS). More recently, obligations of the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP) and the European Union–Vietnam Free Trade Agreement (EVFTA) made Vietnam pay attention to improving its copyright protection. Modernization of Vietnamese Law on Intellectual Property (adopted in 2022) helped the country to develop its intellectual property law regarding digital copyright and enforcement."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-08.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Establishment of the CPTPP"},{"type":"source","text":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comprehensive_and_Progressive_Agreement_for_Trans-Pacific_Partnership"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-09.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"European Union–Vietnam Free Trade Agreement (EVFTA) logo"},{"type":"source","text":"https://policy.trade.ec.europa.eu/eu-trade-relationships-country-and-region/countries-and-regions/viet-nam/eu-viet-nam-agreements_en"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"These legal reforms have helped create a better business atmosphere. Publishers and entertainment firms around the world tend to choose countries where their intellectual property is protected, since such an environment decreases business risks. The better companies think that their investment will not be undermined by piracy, the more they are ready to invest money into making official translations, to establish partnership with local organizations, to launch promotional campaigns, and to present their products to the audience."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The example of the manga and anime industry shows how the process takes place. A number of years ago, Vietnamese people used mainly pirated versions or websites in order to watch Japanese comics and animations. Nowadays, readers can buy licensed Vietnamese versions from official publishers, while streaming services, like Netflix and Crunchyroll, among others, provide legitimate anime content. Even though there is still some piracy in the country, the amount of official products has increased considerably due to copyright laws and increased awareness of consumers."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-10.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Netflix logo"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.netflix.com/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-11.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Crunchyroll Manga App"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.crunchyroll.com/manga"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Digital entertainment also illustrates this phenomenon. International streaming services like Netflix, Disney+, Spotify, and Apple Music are largely based on copyright protection since their profit model is dependent on subscription fees rather than tangible products. The steady progress of these platforms in Southeast Asian countries, including Vietnam, proves that it is now more likely for copyrighted content to be distributed via legitimate means. Also, consumers receive better quality of service, improved subtitles, customer service, and legally distributed content."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-12.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Disney+ logo"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.disneyplus.com/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"However, stronger copyright protection does not serve the interests of foreign firms exclusively. Vietnamese authors, movie producers, musicians, software engineers, and game developers will also profit from the establishment of an adequate intellectual property system. With the development of the domestic creative industries, Vietnamese individuals require the same level of legal security provided for international companies. Adequate copyright laws incentivize people to create something new since they provide a reasonable chance to make money from their work. This leads to a virtuous circle of strengthened legal framework, increased creativity, and additional investments."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-08-13.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Spotify icon"},{"type":"source","text":"https://open.spotify.com/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Nonetheless, copyright regulations should be maintained in a balanced manner since too much stringency can hinder activities like learning, research, criticism, and parodies which are socially beneficial. Modern-day copyright laws provide exceptions through fair use or fair dealing while still protecting commercial usage. In the end, the aim is to ensure that there is an open market where creators, publishers, consumers, and educators benefit from the rules and regulations that are clear and predictable."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Experience in Vietnam indicates that the copyright regime does not only serve as a means of legal protection of intellectual creation. Instead, copyright becomes a mechanism for economic development through investments, innovations, and the development of trust between creators and publishers. Although there is still a problem of copyright infringement, further improvements in enforcing copyright will lead to the sustainable development of the creative industry. Copyright will serve as a guarantee not only for companies but also for consumers who receive high quality goods."}]},{"number":9,"title":"Why Copyright Protection Also Protects the Audience","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"When one speaks of copyright piracy, it is inevitable that people will think of money. The creators do not earn money since the royalties are not theirs anymore; they cannot sell more copies of their books due to copyright violation; the same applies to the producers of movies who see their films pirated without any payment of fees. All of these issues are indeed very important, but there is also another aspect that piracy brings which should be considered. A book or a movie could be badly translated or subtitled by a pirate; or the creator\u0027s work would be cut out from his or her creation without having anyone\u0027s permission. As a result, the audience could get a completely wrong idea about the book or the movie due to the pirated versions."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In my view, the best example is translation. It is not enough to translate words from one language into another. A skillful translator should take into consideration such features of the writing as tone, humor, cultural allusions, character traits, and speech peculiarities of each character. It becomes especially hard if there are some invented words in the original text."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In this respect, the example of the Harry Potter series comes to mind. The author created many characters\u0027 names, jokes, expressions, and magical words which have connection with the English language and British culture. In some cases, these elements are intentionally humorous, while in other cases, they tell something about the character traits. If the translator does not understand the sense of the elements and translates them in his own way, he can spoil the meaning. Thus, sarcastic characters may become serious, jokes may lose their meaning, and some terms may be translated in different ways in different chapters. In such a way, readers who know only the unofficial translation may form the opinion about the author\u0027s writing style partially based on the translator\u0027s interpretation."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Harry Potter novels series.https://www.harrypotter.com/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-09-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The same problem appears to exist in The Lord of the Rings. Tolkien did not write just a fantasy story, but he had been fascinated by languages and invented different language styles, different names, poems, and history for peoples of Middle-earth. It means that translation plays a key role. If the translator ignores the differences and does not keep them in mind, the cultures and the characters start to sound alike instead of sounding as Tolkien wanted them to be."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Fellowship of the Ring(2001)https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0120737/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-09-02.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Films and television are somewhat unique in that many people around the world depend on subtitles or dubbed versions. Professional subtitling is hard work as well. The translator must convey the meaning of the sentence in a restricted number of characters and in a set amount of time. Some humor, culture or tone may have to be modified for it to be understood in another language. Scholars of audiovisual translation have recognized other issues of linguistic correctness, format and adaptation of machine translation to audiovisual translation."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"When it comes to the subtitles produced without authorization, one has to imagine how unreliable things could get. Take a Japanese anime film seen on an illegal streaming service. A character would be extremely respectful while addressing the senior citizen. But the subtitle would say that the character was talking in slang. The joke, which has a Japanese context, would be translated word-for-word and it would seem meaningless. An insult would be exaggerated as the translator wants the dialogue to be more exciting. But none of the alterations has anything to do with the intention of the original author. But people who know no Japanese will not know that. For them, the subtitle is the dialogue. Therefore, platforms such as Crunchyroll and Netflix can keep the meaning while filtering the translations in order not to cause discomfort for audiences."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-09-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Crunchyroll Manga Apphttps://www.crunchyroll.com/manga"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"It can also influence the perception of the characters. The character that was supposed to be polite may appear to be rude. A character that was supposed to be humorous might appear to be either a child or a fool. Even in the case of a political or moral stance of the character, it might turn out to be totally different if there is an improper translation of an essential sentence. This can affect the audience\u0027s perception of the story quite drastically."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"A complex literary work like Dune makes the problem of translation very crucial. Frank Herbert constructed a world where political, religious, ecological and philosophical ideas evolve. Words like Fremen, Bene Gesserit, Kwisatz Haderach, and spice are not merely elements of vocabulary; they are the concepts embedded into the background of the fictional universe. If there is any inconsistency in terminology used for the translation, or an incorrect explanation of a concept, readers may find it hard to understand relations between characters or even the political system of the world. The original story is complex enough as it is.Dune: Part Two(2024)https://www.imdb.com/title/tt15239678/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-09-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Piracy may alter the literary work through editing. The pirated film may be compressed, scenes may be deleted, and audio changed. Sometimes subtitles are included into the video itself making it impossible to separate from the rest of the content. In other cases, changes may be made by distributors according to their taste. The viewers may not even notice that the story is incomplete."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"And here another important aspect of the role of copyright protection arises. Indeed, copyright grants the right-holders the exclusive rights to use the works in various ways, such as reproduction, translation, adaptation, etc. Moreover, international principles of copyright also provide the protection of moral rights, including the protection of the work from certain types of distortions or modifications which could harm the reputation of the author. The World Intellectual Property Organization, for example, considers both the economic and moral rights as crucial for the protection of copyright.World Intellectual Property Organization(WIPO), Genevahttps://www.wipo.int/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-09-05.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"However, the protection of integrity of the copyrighted work is of special importance due to the close connection between creative work and the reputation of its author. In case the translation is performed without authorization and the translated version uses a lot of crude or inappropriate language, then the audience will think that it is the original author who wrote the piece in such a manner. In case subtitles make the characters speak aggressively, then filmmakers or screenwriters are those who are to be blamed for that."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Moreover, this issue becomes especially relevant when the creative work involves cross-cultural communication, for films, books, and video games usually give an insight into the cultures which the audience hardly knows. In case the translated version includes repeated mistranslations of the culturally specific expressions, the audience gets a distorted image of this culture. For example, the Japanese character looks unnecessarily rude since respectful language has been omitted. The same problem can occur with historical films. Bernardo Bertolucci\u0027s The Last Emperor (1987), for example, has been criticized by historians for omitting and altering important aspects of Puyi\u0027s life and modern Chinese history, meaning that audiences unfamiliar with the historical record could mistake the film\u0027s interpretation for a complete representation of the past."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Last Emperor(1987)https://www.theguardian.com/film/2009/apr/15/the-last-emperor"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-09-06.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"It goes without saying that not all official translations are good and that not all fan translations are bad. In fact, there are many very competent and devoted fan translators who dedicate a lot of time to their translation projects. On the other hand, even professional translators can make mistakes. The main difference is accountability: when a book is officially licensed by the publisher, there are certain reasons for them to ensure that the translation is correct and professionally edited; when the film is officially released on some streaming platform, it typically means that some organization has taken care of the translation, subtitling, etc., and can be responsible for its quality.Netflix logohttps://www.netflix.com/"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-09-07.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"When it comes to piracy, this link of accountability gets weaker. Those who upload the movies have nothing to do with the filmmakers, publishers, and translators. They might be more interested in releasing the movie than in controlling its quality. For this reason, stronger copyright protection does not mean just the protection of financial interests of big corporations; it could also serve as an incentive to create official translations and localized versions of films and books."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The producers and publishing houses would have more interest in producing official versions if they knew that those would not be replaced by unauthorized copies in the market. For audiences, it would mean a higher probability of getting what was created by the author or the filmmaker."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In conclusion, piracy is not just an act of stealing a piece of work since it also influences how the work will be presented to the audience. Piracy networks, such as FMovies, which Vietnamese authorities connected to the distribution of about 50,000 movies in illegal ways, show how copyright pieces of work may be replicated and distributed without their originators and distributors being aware of it. Poor translation will affect the character\u0027s personality; wrong subtitles will affect the dialogue of the movie; and unauthorized editing will cut off some part of the plot. Thus, people will form their opinion based on the version of the work, which was not meant by the author. FMovie-a pirate streaming platformhttps://e.vnexpress.net/news/news/hanoi-police-shut-down-site-hosting-50-000-pirated-films-4814197.html"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-09-08.png"}]},{"number":10,"title":"How Illegal Copies Can Put Licensed Series at Risk","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"In cases where copyright piracy is considered, most individuals tend to think about the loss faced by the author and the publishing house. For instance, in the case of a pirated book, there will be a reduction in sales, while for the illegal streaming of a film, there will be less legal viewing. Nonetheless, the copyright piracy issue becomes more complex in the event where a Vietnamese publishing company had to buy the rights to publish the works of a foreign author. In this case, the illegal copy is not just a method through which one can access the same content. It is a product that is directly competing with another product, which has been funded in terms of licensing rights, translation, editing, printing/distribution, and advertising among other activities. Therefore, if the product fails to make any profit, the publishing company will have to come to the conclusion that continuing with the series will not be feasible economically. The victims in such an occurrence are not only the publishing company and copyright holder but also the readers."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-10-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"WingsBook-a Vietnamese publishing company"},{"type":"source","text":"https://wingsbookskimdong.wordpress.com/2018/03/13/ve-wings-books/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The manga industry of Vietnam offers an excellent illustration of how this issue has been generated. Manga from Japan began being imported to Vietnam towards the end of the 1980s, mostly in those cases when the distribution was done without any official copyright contract. Based on a publication that took place in 2024 on the website of the Ministry of Industry and Trade of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, Doraemon was the first manga that was published with copyright in Vietnam in 1996. However, during the subsequent decade or so, a lot of manga in Vietnam had no copyrights, since various companies competed in publishing the same titles. Things started changing more significantly after Vietnam became a member of the Berne Convention in 2004."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-10-02.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Ministry of Industry and Trade of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam official logo"},{"type":"source","text":"https://moit.gov.vn/en/ministry-leader"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The above history is important because purchasing a license alters the economics of publication. A legitimate Vietnamese publishing house does not just get a digital version of a manga and publish it. The publisher must go through negotiation with the owner of copyrights, pay for licenses, translation, editing, Vietnamese version design, printing or online distribution of the Vietnamese version, and marketing and all of that before earning revenue from sales. On the other hand, pirates can duplicate or scan the work and redistribute it without paying anything to the copyright holder, translator, editor or the Vietnamese publishing house. As a result, the products might compete with each other for exactly the same audience but their cost structures will be entirely different."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-10-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"IPM Publishing and Media Joint Stock Company-a Vietnamese publishing house"},{"type":"source","text":"https://ipm.vn/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"A particularly complicated issue relates to serial products. Publishers are not expected to earn the profit from the sale of the first volume of a serial manga. Publishers expect the readers to be interested in purchasing the second volume, third one, and then dozens of volumes over time. In some sense, it is very similar to the way television series work: the value of the investment depends partially on the audience\u0027s willingness to keep following the story. If readers can get each chapter of the story immediately from an unauthorized website, the incentive to buy the official version will fade away."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Vietnamese webtoon industry is an excellent real-life example of such an industry. In 2026, the publishing website operated by the Ministry of Industry and Trade of Vietnam highlighted an issue of copyright infringement involving the webtoons of Comicola. As mentioned by Nguyễn Khánh Dương, the founder of Comicola, at first, the goal of some Korean publishers was to share their work with Vietnamese audiences rather than to increase profits. Nevertheless, as soon as the works were stolen after being published and there were no means of dealing with it, some Korean webtoon services left Vietnam in 2022."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-10-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Comicola official black logo"},{"type":"source","text":"https://vi.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comicola"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Another example is related to the publication of manga in Japan. According to Vietnamese sources, Japanese publishers became more careful regarding license deals with smaller Vietnamese companies because of copyright violations in Vietnam. In one such incident, the website Readism published manga and webtoons by Japanese publishers which were already working with Vietnamese licensees. Such a situation is even more unethical since the pirate site uses the intellectual property of the licensed company without incurring its expenses."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The issue of film piracy is related not only to manga but also to films and TV shows. A Vietnamese distributor might buy the right to screen a film or a TV show, localize and market it, make deals with cinema theatres or streaming websites. In case a high-quality pirate copy is made available soon after the world premiere of the product, some viewers might conclude that there is no need to pay for the official version of the film. It is especially harmful to small distributors who have less financial resources to withstand losses."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"An additional comparison can be found in the video gaming industry. Companies like Nintendo, Capcom, Sony, or CD Projekt Red are spending an enormous amount of money on developing games like The Legend of Zelda, Resident Evil, and Cyberpunk 2077. For a legit publisher, all the licenses and the production costs are a challenge, but for pirates, none of them matter. The same situation arises in books, movies, anime, webtoons, and games; the pirate version has to compete with the official one but without the challenges."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-10-05.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Nintendo Co., Ltd logo used since May 2016."},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.nintendo.com/us/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"There is also a psychological factor here for the readers. Having read a book from a certain series for a long time forms a bond between the reader and the publishing company. People might be attached to a certain translation, a certain version, the book cover or release schedule. Once the company stops publishing the books because of the lack of sales, the reader loses something they cannot restore easily. They have already bought ten volumes and found out that Volume 11 or 12 will not be published in Vietnamese at all."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-10-06.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"CAPCOM official artwork"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.capcom.com/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Such problems can feed off one another, creating a self-reinforcing loop. Consumers notice that the official version is incomplete and thus rely on pirate websites to access the remaining chapters. This leads to poorer sales of the title in question and makes the publisher less likely to license similar books in the future. Rights holders notice weak returns on the market and become less eager to enter the country. The volume of official publications decreases and piracy becomes even more appealing. Changing this dynamic requires doing more than just urging consumers to stop pirating content. It requires creating a market where legitimate publishers can survive."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-10-07.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"CD Projekt Red official introducing creators \u0026 ambassadors artwork"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.cdprojektred.com/en"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"It is for this reason that enforcing copyrights can be good for readers too. In 2026, Vietnamese authorities carried out a series of measures aimed at curbing piracy. According to the 2026 Special 301 Report of the U.S. Trade Representative, those measures included efforts to shut down popular streaming websites such as Fmovies and Y2Mate, as well as e-book sharing platforms in Vietnam. The closure of Vietnam-based HiAnime.to and its mirrors was also mentioned in the report. These actions are important as they create a less welcoming environment for businesses that operate on large-scale copyright violations."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-10-08.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"FMovie-a pirate streaming platformhttps://e.vnexpress.net/news/news/hanoi-police-shut-down-site-hosting-50-000-pirated-films-4814197.html"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Publishing laws in Vietnam also expressly forbid the unauthorized printing, reproduction, and distribution of publications, including the distribution of publications without a legitimate source. However, more significantly, the government has started emphasizing on online copyright protection as a part of creating an open and healthy environment for electronic publishing."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"It is not possible to say that piracy alone would keep every licensed series going forever. A licensed series could be ended owing to poor demand, licensing costs, changing strategy of the rights owner, or internal issues at the publishing house. However, it would be wrong to assume that the cancellation of a series would always be caused by piracy. But nevertheless, piracy makes the publishing business one step harder. If a publisher invests in licensing something, it becomes harder to recoup their money when they face competition from a free version of that series."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In the end, copyright infringement does not stop merely at preventing the free reading of the book. Instead, it is about the protection of the economic system which allows for the creation of official copies of the product. When Vietnamese publishers invest in foreign rights, it is done on the assumption that consumers will buy the product. If piracy stands in the way of that product, then it will cause a chain of consequences all the way down from the publisher to the foreign rights holder to finally reach the consumers themselves. In case of cancellation of a manga series, translation delay, or even the refusal of a foreign company to license its product – it all could become the outcome of what may seem as an innocent act of reading just one chapter."}]},{"number":11,"title":"Cybersecurity and Copyright: Why Online Piracy Is Also a Cybersecurity Problem","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"The topic of piracy is always associated with copyright violations. A film was uploaded to the Internet without proper authorization, some books were illegally distributed via the Internet, and a computer video game was made available via torrent. The primary issue associated with it is related to the loss of revenue by the creator/publisher of a copyrighted product. However, the development of piracy in the digital environment resulted in the emergence of a new problem that needs to be addressed: cybersecurity. Visiting piracy websites and using download sites is risky since such web resources may contain malware, phishing, fraud, identity theft, and other risks. In other words, people who visit piracy websites may not only steal someone\u0027s intellectual property but also compromise their own cybersecurity."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The issue of cybersecurity associated with piracy becomes obvious when it comes to piracy of computer programs. Unlike a movie that can be viewed directly in a browser, pirated software has to be installed on a user\u0027s computer, and this is where the criminals have the chance to manipulate it before its distribution. The hackers can embed malware into crack tools, key generators, installers, and activation tools of the software. After the installation process, the attackers have the opportunity to obtain passwords, personal files, and even control of the computer."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Research carried out by researchers from the National University of Singapore on behalf of Microsoft studied pirated software and the websites involved in distributing them in eight Asian-Pacific countries, including Vietnam. As a result, the research revealed that all tested websites with pirated software download links presented potential threats. In addition, the researchers have established that 61 percent of pirated CDs and DVDs contained malware, and that 92 percent of new computers equipped with non-genuine software were infected with malware. Such numbers are very impressive as they prove the threat to be very real. Pirated software can act as a carrier of malware."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-11-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"NUS study: Cybercriminals exploit pirated software to fuel malware infections in Asia Pacific"},{"type":"source","text":"https://news.microsoft.com/apac/2017/06/21/nus-study-cybercriminals-exploit-pirated-software-fuel-malware-infections-asia-pacific/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Malware in question can be of a particularly dangerous type. Microsoft claims that pirated software can contain Trojans, viruses, spyware, ransomware, backdoors, and other forms of malware. A Trojan, for instance, can pretend to be an ordinary application and provide access to the victim\u0027s computer to an attacker. Other malware can steal credentials of browsers, monitor victims, delete their files, or download other forms of malware. What starts as a possibility to save money can turn into a much more costly problem if personal information and financial resources are stolen."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-11-02.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Bargain or trouble: Cybercrime and non-genuine software"},{"type":"source","text":"https://news.microsoft.com/apac/features/bargain-trouble-cybercrime-non-genuine-software/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"This is becoming true for films, TV series, anime and even sports. While accessing an unlawful streaming website, a user might not have to install any typical executable files, but accessing such websites might lead them to malicious advertisements, misleading pop-ups, phishing sites or downloads. In 2026, the study of the free live sports streaming ecosystem evaluated 260 domains and found serious security and privacy threats, including drive-by downloads and invasive device fingerprinting. Moreover, the researchers found groups of similar domains, which means that illegal streaming can be performed via organized digital infrastructure, not just individual websites."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-11-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Hidden risks in pirated software"},{"type":"source","text":"https://news.microsoft.com/apac/2019/01/08/hidden-risks-in-pirated-software/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"An example of relevance to this situation is the Asia-Pacific region. In June 2026, the Asia Video Industry Association released the results of its research on the topic of illicit streaming services in this region. The study reviewed the risks related to the use of illegal streaming devices, IPTV services, playlist sellers, sharing accounts and third-party streaming applications. It was stated that almost half of the illicit streaming applications reviewed included malware."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-11-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"NEW STUDY REVEALS PIRACY SERVICES ARE EXPOSING MILLIONS OF ASIA-PACIFIC CONSUMERS TO CYBERCRIME, IDENTITY THEFT AND FRAUD"},{"type":"source","text":"https://avia.org/anti-piracy/anti-piracy-reports/"},{"type":"source","text":"https://avia.org/new-study-reveals-piracy-services-are-exposing-millions-of-asia-pacific-consumers-to-cybercrime-identity-theft-and-fraud/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"As is shown by recent examples, criminals can be very quick in making use of popular films. Thus, in August 2026, cybersecurity alerts in connection with a new film called The Odyssey noted that there existed some websites offering free access to the film through various registration and trial pages which in reality collected personal and bank details. Another campaign offered some executable files supposedly representing pirated versions of The Odyssey. According to Bitdefender, these files spread the Lumma Stealer malware which was intended to steal different kinds of sensitive data including browser passwords, payment card data, and cryptocurrencies."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-11-05.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"‘Watch The Odyssey for free online’: scam targets film fans with fake streaming sites"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.theguardian.com/money/2026/aug/09/watch-the-odyssey-for-free-online-scam-film-fans-fake-streaming-sites"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"As one may see, criminals do not necessarily need to invent something attractive from scratch. It is sufficient to exploit the popularity of legitimate entertainment. A new film will attract huge interest, and many will want to view it at once and for free. Consequently, attackers could create a fake \"free download\" or \"free streaming\" service and make use of this desire as part of social engineering."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The support of piracy can also be given through advertising networks. These illegal sites require a business model, and many such sites earn money from advertisements. There can be advertisements which are legal, but there can also be advertisements that can be fraudulent or contain malware. In a report issued in 2025 by the European Union Intellectual Property Office, fraud and malware advertising made up 25% of all monitored advertisements for infringing websites, compared to 14% in 2024. In addition, hundreds of millions of euros were earned from advertising revenue from monitored infringing websites and apps throughout the world."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-11-06.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Online Advertising on IPR-Infringing Websites and Apps 2025"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.euipo.europa.eu/nl/publications/online-advertising-on-ipr-infringing-websites-and-apps-2025"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"This forms what can be termed as an illicit digital ecosystem. Here the pirate website offers the copyrighted material illegally. The advertising network earns money from it. The users contribute the traffic. The cybercriminals can exploit this traffic through advertisements that are fraudulent, fake downloads, phishing or even data stealing. It is possible that in some cases, even payment providers, hosting services, domain registrars, and other infrastructure providers can form a part of this wider ecosystem."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The Digital Citizens Alliance has referred to another problem which links piracy, advertising, and ransomware. It turned out that users visiting movie piracy websites might be exposed to malware advertisements aimed at luring them into downloading malware, including ransomware. Hence, the issue is not only about loss of money one should have spent on the services of a legitimate streaming website. There is a risk of losing personal files or even having private data stolen from the device."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-11-07.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"From Piracy to Ads to Ransomware: How Illicit Actors Use Digital Ads on Piracy Sites to Profit by Harming Internet Users"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.digitalcitizensalliance.org/issues/unholy-triangle-report/"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"This cyber security risk affects not only individual users but also businesses. Just imagine a situation when a businessperson downloads a cracked version of a professional application for the work onto a company\u0027s computer. In case the software used by pirates has been compromised by a backdoor or credential stealing malware, there is a possibility of a company-wide security breach."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"This is why copyright enforcement increasingly intersects with cybersecurity. Copyright owners can detect unauthorized websites and demand that the content be taken down; however, a more comprehensive approach would include domain registrars, hosting companies, advertising networks, financial institutions, search engines, cybersecurity experts, and law-enforcement agencies. INTERPOL specifically points out the risk of malware infections and stealing private data through pirate websites and peer-to-peer networks, adding the risk of using fake payment methods."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-11-08.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Accessing free or cheap content is not the bargain you think it is!"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.interpol.int/en/Crimes/Illicit-goods/Shop-safely/Digital-piracy"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Yet, the enforcement of copyright laws shouldn’t lead to classifying any person that finds themselves visiting pirate sites as a cybercriminal. It’s very important to distinguish between the consumer and an organized entity that commercially distributes copyrighted material. The latter category especially includes those that operate large-scale websites, monetize the stolen content, distribute malware, steal private information, or commit other crimes. However, at the same time, the consumers must be provided with affordable and easily accessible legitimate services. If they exist and are inexpensive, there won’t be many reasons for people to visit suspicious sites."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"In conclusion, online piracy has developed from simply being an act of making copies of books, films, music, and video games without authorization. This kind of piracy might become intertwined with malware dissemination, phishing, extortion, data theft, adware, and cyber crimes in general. The one looking for a movie to download for free is trying to save money, while the one owning the site uses traffic for financial gain or to spread malware."}]},{"number":12,"title":"From Copyright Infringement Investigation: How Cyber Police Track Online Pirates","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"Online copyright infringement may seem quite simple at first glance: a user uploads a movie, copies a football game, shares a book or a software program, and potentially hundreds of thousands, or even millions, of people have access to such content. However, behind the scenes, there might be websites, servers, advertising networks, payment systems, social media channels, technical support personnel, and various individuals with different roles involved. In such a case, online copyright infringement becomes an organized activity of illegal business in cyberspace. So, the next logical question is how law enforcement agencies are able to establish who commits such crimes when everything is done online. Vietnamese practice shows that cyber and economic police tend to use various methods including online investigation, money trail, international cooperation, and coordinated raids."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The first step is to establish that copyright infringement has occurred and to understand how the operation works. Copyright holders, publishers, TV stations, cybersecurity experts or government bodies could discover such facts about infringement of their rights. Thus, in May 2026, the Vietnamese Ministry of Public Security conducted a national campaign against serious violations of intellectual property rights and specifically ordered it to investigate and close large online websites that illegally distribute movies, music, games, and TV programs."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-12-01.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Nationwide campaign to prevent and address intellectual property rights infringements from May 7 to May 30, 2026-The Vietnamese Ministry of Public Security"},{"type":"source","text":"https://bocongan.gov.vn/bai-viet/ra-quan-ngan-chan-xu-ly-hanh-vi-xam-pham-quyen-so-huu-tri-tue-tren-toan-quoc-tu-07-5-30-5-2026-1778054419"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"However, this may not be enough since closing one website does not mean identifying those responsible. Sometimes a piracy network uses multiple websites, social media profiles, systems, and businesses. This is why investigators have to reveal how such organizations operate based on their visible websites. Evidence may involve digital materials collected according to legal means such as website content, account information, transactions, correspondence, devices, and others. Investigators aim at building a connection between the illegal content and the individuals involved in the creation, management, financing, or gaining profit from it."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"One example of the use of digital forensics is the 2024 investigation in Hanoi, Vietnam of the FMovies network. Vietnamese authorities found out that there were about 50,000 movies suspected of copyright infringement in the system. After that, Hanoi police initiated a criminal case against two individuals by applying Article 225 of the Criminal Code. In this situation, the size of the website played an important role since the scale of the case implied that it could not be limited to one individual watching some movies with friends."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"FMovie-a pirate streaming platformhttps://e.vnexpress.net/news/news/hanoi-police-shut-down-site-hosting-50-000-pirated-films-4814197.html"},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-12-02.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Hence, one of the most essential methods used in contemporary cyber investigations is connecting various pieces of evidence. It is obvious that just having the address of a website is not enough to determine the guilty party. Specialists must find out whose accounts are controlled, who owns the technical resources, who publishes the material in question, and finally, who earns the profit from this activity. That is why copyright investigation may include not only cybercrime specialists but also economic policemen."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Financial aspects may be of great significance in such cases. There are many well-known sites of internet piracy that do not exist only because of ideological reasons. These sites earn money via advertising, subscription, donation, affiliate programs, etc. If the site has millions of visitors, even a small amount of money earned from advertisements will add up to a considerable sum."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Another significant case was reported in Vietnam in July 2026. As stated by the Ministry of Public Security and Government News Portal, the investigation was conducted with the help of the information provided by American authorities, including the Alliance for Creativity and Entertainment and Homeland Security Investigations. The investigation revealed an illegal enterprise that operated over 100 websites and pirated over 26,000 movies from 2020 to April 2026. It is said that these websites earned about VND 308.4 billion via advertising revenues. Of these, four people were charged for copyright-related crimes and money laundering, and three others were charged for copyright infringement."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-12-03.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Piracy ring accused of hosting 26,000 illegal movieshttps://vietnamnews.vn/society/1784574/film-piracy-ring-accused-of-hosting-26-000-illegal-movies.html"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"This case clearly explains the importance of financial investigation. Investigators would have seen the pirated movies on the websites had they focused only on them. However, the investigation through the financial aspect allows examining the process of earning money and hiding it and using it to buy certain property. This case can be considered as going beyond copyright infringement to financial investigation."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Cooperation among various law enforcement agencies is another crucial strategy. Online copyright infringement is not limited to a certain type of offense. A website could be distributing movies illegally, as well as offering gambling. Money earned by a certain piracy network through advertisements can be hidden after that. A football streaming service could be violating broadcasting laws while enabling gambling."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-12-04.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"30 defendants charged in connection with the illegal \"Xoi Lac\" streaming network-a cooperation between Cybersecurity Department, local police and copyright investigation of Vietnam"},{"type":"source","text":"https://bocongan.gov.vn/bai-viet/khoi-to-30-bi-can-trong-duong-day-web-lau-xoi-lac-1772683363"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Cross-border cooperation is yet another necessary component. The Internet knows no national borders. The copyright owner can reside in the United States, the website operator in Vietnam, server infrastructure can be from another country, and ads and payment services can be international. The July 2026 film-piracy case demonstrates that the information provided by U.S. agencies played its role in the Vietnamese investigation."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Physical evidence can be used by investigators in order to verify information obtained during online investigations. It is not true that cyber investigations mean sitting behind a computer for a long time. Once enough evidence is gathered, and all necessary conditions are met, it becomes possible to conduct searches and confiscate computers, mobiles, data storages, livestreaming tools, documents, and financial records. These materials will be able to show who had managed the system and what were their functions as can be seen in a number of piracy Microsoft Windows cases."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/episodes/episode-12-05.png"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Vietnam Launches Criminal Investigation into Copyright Infringement of Computer Software"},{"type":"source","text":"https://www.bocongan.gov.vn/bai-viet/cong-an-tinh-phu-tho-khoi-to-vu-an-dau-tien-tren-ca-nuoc-ve-xam-pham-quyen-tac-gia-doi-voi-phan-mem-may-tinh-1781166247"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"However, it should be noted that it is necessary to differentiate between copyright infringement and criminal copyright infringement. Not all those who watch an illegal video or download an unlawful copy would face criminal charges for that. Criminal responsibility for such actions depends on the circumstances, proof, magnitude, commercial intent, and requirements of the statute. In Vietnam, according to article 225 of the Criminal Code, there is a basis for criminal liability for certain copyright infringement offenses. The investigators must identify the elements of the crime, and not prove the presence of copyrighted content online."}]}];